q-50411" :question/id #uuid "18df67e9-e8a6-53fd-b815-f8c50e7fd68d" :question/math-academy-id "q-50411" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2{sec}^{2}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=2{sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=2{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =⟨{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-50411/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-50411"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-349470/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "319f4de3-4270-5152-a033-34aa45cd1a69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-349470/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "78bc53ad-0327-5610-8ddf-c5d25c189594" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-349470/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c566ab8-7080-51e1-8818-8c8bd6d599d0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-349470/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-349470/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-349470/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-349470/field-2/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "726da3c0-bab6-5518-a424-d15bd34f0bae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-349470/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "e9af2f6c-85f0-5b58-a303-10540c542ab4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-349470/field-2/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer-field/choices ["q-349470/field-2/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-349470" :question/id #uuid "3afbda33-c7c2-580e-b2cd-cf4f091a3552" :question/math-academy-id "q-349470" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨4+3{t}^{2},\\,4{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}-1⟩,$ what is ${r}^{′}(1)?$\n\n${r}^{′}(1)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=4+3{t}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=6t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(1)=6\\cdot 1=6.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=4{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}-1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=12{t}^{2}+6t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(1)=12\\cdot {1}^{2}+6\\cdot 1=18.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(1) & =⟨{x}^{′}(1),\\,{y}^{′}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,18⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-349470/field-1" "q-349470/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-349470"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-347619/field-1/39e2cdcdf3c2e8355f9924af3c7d402b675f9ca92935e57ef42e934dd826a0a4" :answer/id #uuid "6673f5f5-518f-515d-a011-7e4f467a67b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3e^{3t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347619/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "edca0f77-c72b-54f0-88eb-385166031536" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347619/field-1/39e2cdcdf3c2e8355f9924af3c7d402b675f9ca92935e57ef42e934dd826a0a4" :answer-field/choices ["q-347619/field-1/39e2cdcdf3c2e8355f9924af3c7d402b675f9ca92935e57ef42e934dd826a0a4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347619/field-2/23681146692c2bcfc79488e95e10dc17680c2701faa40af1fe50477f57b098dd" :answer/id #uuid "56ee9c24-baa8-540d-be2e-dcc2dddb01c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347619/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "65f326d8-0d4f-5a17-8877-2a0bbeacdc4c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347619/field-2/23681146692c2bcfc79488e95e10dc17680c2701faa40af1fe50477f57b098dd" :answer-field/choices ["q-347619/field-2/23681146692c2bcfc79488e95e10dc17680c2701faa40af1fe50477f57b098dd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347619" :question/id #uuid "5d77ce32-0cd3-5cc9-930e-2d996cff969e" :question/math-academy-id "q-347619" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨{e}^{3t}-4,\\,6\\sqrt{t}⟩,$ what is ${r}^{′}(t)?$\n\n${r}^{′}(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)={e}^{3t}-4,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{e}^{3t}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=6\\sqrt{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{6}{2\\sqrt{t}}=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{e}^{3t},\\,\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-347619/field-1" "q-347619/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347619"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-350217/field-1/779a00b71eaa6f89e3598b796b3c5f7fb4a7a9803683d0889a6246eabb7a09c0" :answer/id #uuid "3f2cf53f-0a03-5492-badf-23567511c513" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{289}{8}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350217/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d016461-d01f-5e87-b800-716e6141c9ae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-350217/field-1/779a00b71eaa6f89e3598b796b3c5f7fb4a7a9803683d0889a6246eabb7a09c0" :answer-field/choices ["q-350217/field-1/779a00b71eaa6f89e3598b796b3c5f7fb4a7a9803683d0889a6246eabb7a09c0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-350217" :question/id #uuid "b3f67fdf-42e5-51a2-b0ea-ed2cd345e814" :question/math-academy-id "q-350217" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\sqrt{1-t},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩,$ what is $|{r}^{′}(-1)|?$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$|{r}^{′}(-1)|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\sqrt{1-t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-t}},\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(-1)=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-(-1)}}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=3{t}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=6t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(-1)=6(-1)=-6.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(-1) & =⟨{x}^{′}(-1),\\,{y}^{′}(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}},\\,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{r}^{′}(-1)| & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}})}^{2}+{(-6)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{8}+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{289}{8}} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-350217/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-350217"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130398/selection/66c16de5f74fd839f530ef0ff1d8d805f2ba23fed184f6f54cac19565efb3481" :answer/id #uuid "af21df73-b3d9-5292-8f71-844f46604c4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({e}^{t}+{sec}^{2}⁡t)\\,j+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130398/selection/a1b37d75888ccfcfdb962eaba5a0e96915a23d8393e4e06031c10a5bd1bfb195" :answer/id #uuid "4eeda593-52b3-5ae3-a94d-4d02bff9b1c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡t\\,i+(2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t)\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130398/selection/7006850ad3b1f6b1b17a6ecf57151dd35f1405509b0a28a63a0b1080bc4337cd" :answer/id #uuid "de380a5d-7be8-5bfa-9e9e-377458e79fe4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({e}^{t}+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t)\\,i+(2{t}^{2}+t)\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130398/selection/8d315d3ef4c4454b5249978fc4ab9937d58457c1156509a18e3ab4dbae494d22" :answer/id #uuid "6a693f00-9cea-5f7c-812f-87f83dbbad5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({e}^{t}+{sec}^{2}⁡t)\\,i-2\\,j+(2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t)\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130398/selection/e626daed599864845a787e8e47f5364dc25eeeab87e49c95d563e0703c66d85a" :answer/id #uuid "0087253a-a7b9-5ed7-9742-ef999d49418f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({e}^{t}+{sec}^{2}⁡t)\\,i+(2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t)\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130398/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2ad567c9-78b9-5f1a-921f-cc2f5ea3642c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130398/selection/e626daed599864845a787e8e47f5364dc25eeeab87e49c95d563e0703c66d85a" :answer-field/choices ["q-130398/selection/66c16de5f74fd839f530ef0ff1d8d805f2ba23fed184f6f54cac19565efb3481" "q-130398/selection/a1b37d75888ccfcfdb962eaba5a0e96915a23d8393e4e06031c10a5bd1bfb195" "q-130398/selection/7006850ad3b1f6b1b17a6ecf57151dd35f1405509b0a28a63a0b1080bc4337cd" "q-130398/selection/8d315d3ef4c4454b5249978fc4ab9937d58457c1156509a18e3ab4dbae494d22" "q-130398/selection/e626daed599864845a787e8e47f5364dc25eeeab87e49c95d563e0703c66d85a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130398" :question/id #uuid "e39e9ea0-2d4a-5e70-a49b-0f623f92f7d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-130398" :question/problem "Find the derivative of  $f(t)=({e}^{t}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)\\,i-5\\,j+{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,k$ with respect to $t.$" :question/worked-solution "We find the derivative of $f(t)$  by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)k \\\\  & =({e}^{t}+{sec}^{2}⁡t)\\,i-0\\,j+(2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t)\\,k \\\\  & =({e}^{t}+{sec}^{2}⁡t)\\,i+(2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130398/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130398"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130400/selection/07f1ba515579ecb69f6b990173234172fa6ddee95ed371098cb8c44a58284bf9" :answer/id #uuid "4c2d4f03-ab6e-5635-9b14-14ab3bc107dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{20}{{t}^{5}} \\\\ 2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130400/selection/2f8e8718746e655181e3d67d8a72c5ae1a03927ff1407b67ee56acb0b5d7b43a" :answer/id #uuid "c2d4415e-4f83-5e6c-86bb-48907f85f5aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{20}{{t}^{5}} \\\\ 2t\\op